course: dictionary
lesson: 9315
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Spell has more than one meaning, so context tells you which one the author means. «Height is spelled h-e-i-g-h-t, like weight.» Here spell means to write the letters of a word in the right order, because the sentence is about letters.
explain: «Vikings wrote with runes, and runes were mostly writing, not magic spells.» Here a spell is a set of magic words in a story. The clue is magic: witches and wizards cast spells, and runes were not magic.
explain: Weather reports use spell too: «a cold spell» and «a dry spell» are short periods of time. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: To spell a word means to say or write its letters in the right order.
fact: A spell is a set of magic words that makes something happen in stories.
fact: A spell can also be a short period of time, like «a dry spell».
fact: To spell something out means to explain it very clearly.
fact: To spell trouble means to be a sign that something bad will happen.
exercise: «Pharaoh is spelled P-H-A-R-A-O-H.» What does spelled mean in this sentence? | Cast a magic spell over the king | Lasted for a short period | *Said or wrote its letters in the right order | Explained very clearly
exercise: The witch raised her wand and cast a spell, and the frog turned into a prince. What is a spell here? | Letters written in the right order | *A set of magic words that makes something happen | A tall tower in a castle | A short period of dry weather
exercise: «We had a dry spell all summer, and not one drop of rain fell.» What does spell mean here? | Letters in the right order | *A short period of time | Magic words | To explain very clearly
test: «Mum asked me to spell out the plan, so I explained each step very clearly.» What does spell out mean? | *To explain something very clearly | To cast a magic spell | To end something quickly | To write the letters of a word
test: «The dark clouds and the wind spell trouble for our picnic.» What does spell trouble mean? | Letters that are spelt wrong | *A sign that something bad will happen | Magic words that cause a storm | A short period of rain
exam: Sofia reads «Height is spelled h-e-i-g-h-t, like weight.» Which meaning of spell fits best? | *To say or write the letters of a word in the right order | A short period of time | To explain something very clearly | A set of magic words in a story
